  "query_preview": "..\nSynopsis:\nA couple cut-off lows exist over the region. The one just to our\nnorth is expected to drift east into Manitoba today. The other low\nis dropping SW from British Columbia and is expected to remain \noff the Pac NW coast for the next few days.\n\nThere is a decent chance of fog occurring tonight into the morning\ntomorrow, but it is not guaranteed to happen.\n\nWith the upper low over BC, the zonal flow today and tomorrow \nwill become more meridional as a ridge over the Eastern Montana is\ninduced. This won't boost temps much but will send moisture in on\nFriday in the form of clouds.\n\nPrecip chances do increase over the weekend with the highest\nchances for rain coming Sunday night. THere is uncertainty of how\nmuch precipitation will fall.\n\nClearing is expected behind the system early next week with an\nupper ridge bringing in drier conditions.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo deviations from the NBM.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence in temperatures this week,\nand moderate confidence in fog occurring tonight and lasting\nthrough mid morning tomorrow.\n\nThere is low confidence in precipitation type and amounts this\nweekend.",
